#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: restock anything
#> pause: 45
#> must: 1 apples 12
#> must: (note) figs and grapes are seasonal
#> must: (note) restock anything under 10
#> must: 8 lemons 22
#> not: cherries
#> source: note.txt
# 15. r and R. Sheet: "r file" appends the file after the pattern; "R file" (GNU) appends
# one line of it per match. Paths are relative to the work dir shown at the top.
# The whole note comes after lemons; R takes a line from the note for apples and the
# next for bananas. w and W write to a file; W writes only the first line of the space.
# Try: change R to r and the note lands in full after apples and again after bananas.
#ARGS -n
/[0-9] [ab]/{p;R tutorials/sed/3-krumins-cheat-sheet/data/note.txt
}
$p
$r tutorials/sed/3-krumins-cheat-sheet/data/note.txt

#DATA
1 apples 12
2 bananas 30
3 cherries 7
4 dates 16
5 figs 25
6 grapes 40
7 kiwis 18
8 lemons 22
